{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Query results sometimes need to become a report. Files help summarize shipping or compare amounts, while evaluators also want to manage who downloaded which data for what purpose."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This time I used QueryPie’s "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "SQL Export Request"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " to export an order summary. The developer submitted SQL and a reason, obtained approval, then downloaded the file. Workflow connected the request, approval, and execution result."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The database contains fictional lab orders connected to Community Edition. No actual customer data was used."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Selecting Only the Report’s Required Fields"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The task was a shipping report for three orders. It needed ID, status, and amount, not customer names or contacts, so those fields were excluded."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The SQL selected only order_id, status, and total_amount from orders, restricted to IDs 4001–4003."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeBlock",
      "attrs": {
        "language": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SELECT order_id, status, total_amount\nFROM orders_control.orders\nWHERE order_id BETWEEN 4001 AND 4003\nORDER BY order_id;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Expressing the export scope in SQL lets approvers inspect precisely what is requested, rather than relying on ‘I need order data.’"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. Defining the Approver and Recipient"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In Approval Rules, I created Orders Lab - Export Approval with type SQL Export Request."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Demo Approver approves; Demo Developer executes. The developer requests data, then exports it after review. Self-approval was disabled."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/sql-export/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. Separate approver and executor in the SQL Export Request rule.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. Separate approver and executor in the SQL Export Request rule."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Roles can also govern downloading: the reviewer and the person using the file can be assigned to match the task."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. Submitting SQL and Purpose Together"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I opened Workflow → SQL Export Request as the developer. The rule populated the designated approver and executor."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I titled it ‘Export order summary for shipping report,’ selected Orders Control Lab and orders_control, and entered the SQL using Query Result. Both approval and execution deadlines were the lab day."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/sql-export/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. Export request with approver, executor, and connection.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. Export request with approver, executor, and connection."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The reason specified IDs, statuses, and amounts only, excluding names, phone numbers, and emails. After submission, In Progress showed both approval and execution as Pending."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/sql-export/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Approval and execution each show their pending state.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Approval and execution each show their pending state."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. The Approver Checks the Actual Export SQL"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Demo Approver opened Received Requests and reviewed the SQL, business reason, and execution deadline."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/sql-export/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. Reviewing requested columns, order range, and reason.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. Reviewing requested columns, order range, and reason."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I verified contacts were absent from the SQL, approved, and noted that the shipping-report export was allowed without contact details."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Business purpose and SQL remained together in the approval record, giving a starting point for later questions about why data was exported."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. The Download Contains the Three Requested Orders"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "As the developer, I opened the approved request under Executions → To Do, clicked Execute, and chose CSV with column names in the first row."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The download completed, and Results retained "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "3 Rows selected"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " as the execution result."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/sql-export/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. Results shows the executed SQL and returned row count.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. Results shows the executed SQL and returned row count."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I opened export.csv inside the ZIP. Its header was order_id, status, total_amount, followed by orders 4001, 4002, and 4003 with statuses and amounts: exactly the three requested columns and rows."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/sql-export/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. The downloaded CSV contains the approved SQL results.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. The downloaded CSV contains the approved SQL results."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The completed request moved to Executions → Done with status "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Success"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", together with requester, request time, and update time."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/sql-export/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. The completed export remains available with Success status.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 7. The completed export remains available with Success status."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "6. Evidence for the Work of Obtaining Data"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SQL Export Request connects the work before and after file creation: the user submits SQL and reason, the approver reviews the contents, and the executor downloads from the approved request."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "It is easy to demonstrate its value to evaluators: "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "who requested what, who approved it, and whether execution succeeded"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " can all be followed through request and result screens."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Three orders to CSV was a small task, but it verified approval and execution records for data exports. It showed how everyday database work, such as report preparation, can be managed within QueryPie."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
